From 15fe7b084c9c61337ae14db18838d9867e4ae670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:22:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 27/32] fix(desktop): suspend top-center toasts and statusbar
 during coarse narrow reveals
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Q1.A: the top-center notification banner (fixed, over-modal) painted over a
revealed narrow drawer's first rows on phones. Suspend the stack for the
reveal's lifetime — the store (counts, dismiss timers) is untouched, so the
banner returns exactly as it was when the drawer closes.

Q1.B: the in-flow statusbar and the drawer fought over the bottom edge while
revealed. Unmount the statusbar for the reveal's lifetime (same unmount
semantics as the toggle-off path) and align the composer dock to the new
shared --drawer-bottom-align variable so the drawer's last row and the dock
share one baseline. Both gated on coarse pointer + active reveal; fine
pointers and reveal-inactive coarse layouts are pixel-identical.
